; nodeid-interning-band.fk — a NodeID is identity-by-content: eq of two mints
; of the same four coordinates answers 1, whichever value node carried them;
; any differing coordinate answers 0; a nodeid never equals an int, a list,
; or nothing. value_eq agrees with eq on both sides.
;
; Witnessed into the kernel 2026-08-30 (the tag-102 heal): before it, equal
; coordinates compared by value-node handle and answered 0 — eq never asked
; fk_neq, which had carried the kind-3 coordinate law all along. The same
; heal lit the turnwheel band's held-out equivalence gate (4194303 ->
; 8388607, its own declared Expected) from a distance. Four-way as of
; 2026-08-30: the go, rust, and ts proof walkers carry make_nodeid and the
; same eq law, so all four arms witness this band.
;
; Expected: 127
; preludes: form-stdlib/core.fk
(do
    (let a (make_nodeid 7 3 2 91))
    (let b (make_nodeid 7 3 2 91))
    (let c (make_nodeid 7 3 2 92))
    (sum (list
        (if (eq a b) 1 0)
        (if (eq a c) 0 2)
        (if (eq a 42) 0 4)
        (if (eq a (list 7 3 2 91)) 0 8)
        (if (eq a (nothing)) 0 16)
        (if (value_eq a b) 32 0)
        (if (value_eq a c) 0 64))))
